{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "sabil-api-v1-collection",
    "name": "Sabil Financial Identity API",
    "description": "Complete API collection for the Sabil Financial Identity Backend.\n\n## 3-Step User Flow\n1. **Step 1 — Auth**: Send OTP → Verify OTP → get `access_token`\n2. **Step 2 — KYC**: Upload ID photo + selfie (+ optional manual fields)\n3. **Step 3 — Credit**: Upload bank statements / receipts → get credit score\n\n## Authentication\nAll protected endpoints require:\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer {{access_token}}\n```\nThe token is automatically set after a successful `POST /auth/verify-otp`.\n\n## Dev Bypass\n- Phone: `+96742424242`\n- OTP code: `7744`\n\n## Base URL\nSet the `base_url` variable to your server (default: `http://localhost:8000`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL of the Sabil backend server"
    },
    {
      "key": "api_prefix",
      "value": "/api/v1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "API version prefix"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JWT access token — auto-set by the verify-otp request"
    },
    {
      "key": "dev_phone",
      "value": "+96742424242",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Dev bypass phone number (always passes OTP)"
    },
    {
      "key": "dev_otp",
      "value": "7744",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Dev bypass OTP code"
    },
    {
      "key": "user_id",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Current user ID — auto-set after verify-otp"
    },
    {
      "key": "target_user_id",
      "value": "2",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Target user ID for admin operations or wallet transfers"
    },
    {
      "key": "transaction_id",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Parsed transaction ID for correction/resolve endpoints"
    },
    {
      "key": "country_code",
      "value": "YE",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ISO country code for the user (e.g. YE, SA, TR, AE)"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [

    {
      "name": "🔐 Auth",
      "description": "Step 1 of the user flow. Send OTP → Verify OTP → receive access_token.\n\nDev bypass: phone `+96742424242`, code `7744`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has message', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('phone_number');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('expires_in');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone_number\": \"{{dev_phone}}\",\n  \"country_code\": \"{{country_code}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/auth/send-otp",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "send-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Sends a one-time password to the provided phone number.\n\n**Dev bypass:** phone `+96742424242` always receives code `7744`.\n\nRate limited: 3 requests/minute."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify OTP → Set Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has access_token', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.token_type).to.eql('bearer');",
                  "  // Auto-set collection variables",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', String(body.user.id));",
                  "  console.log('Token saved. User ID:', body.user.id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"phone_number\": \"{{dev_phone}}\",\n  \"otp_code\": \"{{dev_otp}}\",\n  \"full_name\": \"Ahmed Sultan\",\n  \"country_code\": \"{{country_code}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/auth/verify-otp",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "verify-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the OTP code. On success:\n- Creates a new account (first time) or logs in the existing user\n- Returns `access_token` + user profile\n- **Auto-sets** `access_token` and `user_id` collection variables\n\n**Dev bypass:** phone `+96742424242` with code `7744` always succeeds."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login via Firebase Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id_token\": \"<firebase-id-token-from-client-sdk>\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Backward-compatible Firebase token login. Verifies a Firebase ID token and returns the user profile. Creates a new account and wallet on first login.\n\nUse `/auth/send-otp` + `/auth/verify-otp` for the phone OTP flow instead."
          }
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "👤 Users",
      "description": "User profile management. Most endpoints require a valid Bearer token.\nAdmin-only endpoints require `is_admin=true` on the user account.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get My Profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has user fields', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('id');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('phone_number');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('onboarding_step');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the profile of the currently authenticated user."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Onboarding Status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has onboarding fields', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('onboarding_step');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('phone_verified');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('next_step');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('next_step_url');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users/me/onboarding-status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users", "me", "onboarding-status"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the current onboarding step and what the user needs to do next.\n\nSteps:\n- `0` — Phone not verified\n- `1` — Phone verified, KYC not started\n- `2` — KYC submitted\n- `3` — Financial documents uploaded"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update My Profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"full_name\": \"Ahmed Sultan Ahmed\",\n  \"email\": \"ahmed@example.com\",\n  \"country_code\": \"YE\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Updates non-sensitive profile information. All fields are optional — only provided fields are updated.\n\nRate limited: 5 requests/minute."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete My Account",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users", "me"]
            },
            "description": "⚠️ Permanently deletes the authenticated user's account and all associated data.\n\nReturns `204 No Content` on success.\n\nRate limited: 1 request/minute."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[Admin] List All Users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users?skip=0&limit=20",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "skip",      "value": "0",    "description": "Pagination offset" },
                { "key": "limit",     "value": "20",   "description": "Max results (default 100)" },
                { "key": "email",     "value": "",     "description": "Filter by email (optional)", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "phone",     "value": "",     "description": "Filter by phone (optional)", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "is_active", "value": "true", "description": "Filter by active status (optional)", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Admin only.** Retrieves a paginated and filtered list of all users."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[Admin] Get User by ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users/{{target_user_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{target_user_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "**Admin only.** Retrieves any user's profile by their internal ID."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[Admin] Update Any User",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"is_active\": true,\n  \"full_name\": \"Updated Name\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/users/{{target_user_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{target_user_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "**Admin only.** Updates any user's profile or status."
          }
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "🪪 KYC — Identity Verification",
      "description": "Step 2 of the user flow. Upload a government-issued ID photo and a live selfie.\n\nThe pipeline runs:\n1. Image validation (MIME, size, decodability)\n2. Face detection (Haar cascade + DeepFace)\n3. Liveness check (sharpness + frequency analysis)\n4. OCR extraction (EasyOCR / Tesseract fallback)\n5. Document authenticity heuristics\n6. Face matching (VGG-Face via DeepFace)\n7. Duplicate ID detection\n\nAll file uploads use `multipart/form-data`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit KYC Verification",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Has KYC fields', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('id');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('status');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('face_match_score');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('liveness_score');",
                  "  console.log('KYC status:', body.status);",
                  "  console.log('Face match:', body.face_match_score);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "id_card",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Government-issued ID photo (JPEG/PNG/WebP, max 10MB)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "selfie",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Live selfie — face must be clearly visible"
                },
                {
                  "key": "id_type",
                  "value": "passport",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Document type: national_id | passport | drivers_license | residence_permit"
                },
                {
                  "key": "full_name",
                  "value": "SALIH SAMIER S OTMAN",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) Full name as on document — overrides OCR"
                },
                {
                  "key": "id_number",
                  "value": "AE205783",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) Passport/ID number — overrides OCR"
                },
                {
                  "key": "issue_date",
                  "value": "2024-07-23",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) Document issue date YYYY-MM-DD — overrides OCR"
                },
                {
                  "key": "expiry_date",
                  "value": "2032-07-22",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) Document expiry date YYYY-MM-DD — overrides OCR"
                },
                {
                  "key": "country",
                  "value": "LY",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) ISO country code of document (e.g. LY, YE, SA)"
                },
                {
                  "key": "nationality",
                  "value": "Libyan",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) Nationality string — overrides OCR"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/kyc/verify",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["kyc", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "**Step 2** — Upload a government-issued ID photo and a live selfie.\n\nOptional manual fields override OCR extraction when provided. This is useful when OCR quality is poor.\n\nReturns a `KYCResponse` with:\n- `status`: `verified` | `pending` | `rejected`\n- `face_match_score`: 0.0–1.0\n- `liveness_score`: Laplacian variance\n- `authenticity_score`: 0.0–1.0\n- `rejection_reason`: if rejected\n\nRate limited: 3 requests/minute."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Resubmit KYC After Rejection",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "id_card",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Updated photo of identity document"
                },
                {
                  "key": "selfie",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "New live selfie"
                },
                {
                  "key": "id_type",
                  "value": "passport",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Document type: national_id | passport | drivers_license | residence_permit"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/kyc/resubmit",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["kyc", "resubmit"]
            },
            "description": "Re-attempt verification after a `REJECTED` status. Only allowed when current status is `rejected` or `resubmitted`.\n\nCapped by `KYC_MAX_RESUBMISSIONS` setting (default: 30).\n\nRate limited: 2 requests/minute."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get KYC Status",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Has status field', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(['verified','pending','rejected','resubmitted']).to.include(body.status);",
                  "  console.log('KYC status:', body.status, '| Summary:', body.verification_summary);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/kyc/status",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["kyc", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the most recent active KYC record with full verification details including `verification_summary` (human-readable one-liner)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get KYC History",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/kyc/history",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["kyc", "history"]
            },
            "description": "Returns all past KYC attempts including rejections, ordered newest first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Debug — Inspect OCR Output",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "id_card",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "ID card image to inspect"
                },
                {
                  "key": "id_type",
                  "value": "passport",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Document type"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/kyc/debug-ocr",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["kyc", "debug-ocr"]
            },
            "description": "Upload an ID image and see exactly what OCR extracted — raw tokens, field extraction results, MRZ parsing, variant scores.\n\n**No data is saved.** Use to diagnose OCR quality issues."
          }
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "🛡️ Admin — KYC",
      "description": "Admin-only KYC management endpoints. Require `is_admin=true` on the authenticated user.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "[Admin] List KYC Applications",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/admin/kyc/list?page=1&page_size=20",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "kyc", "list"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page",         "value": "1",        "description": "Page number (default 1)" },
                { "key": "page_size",    "value": "20",       "description": "Results per page (max 100)" },
                { "key": "status",       "value": "pending",  "description": "Filter: pending | verified | rejected | resubmitted", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "expired_only", "value": "false",    "description": "Only expired VERIFIED records", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "user_id",      "value": "",         "description": "Filter by user ID", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "id_number",    "value": "",         "description": "Search by ID number (blind index)", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Admin only.** Paginated list of all KYC applications with optional filters."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "[Admin] Submit Manual Review",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"note\": \"Documents verified manually. All checks passed.\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/admin/kyc/{{target_user_id}}/review",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "kyc", "{{target_user_id}}", "review"]
            },
            "description": "**Admin only.** Approve or reject a KYC application manually.\n\nSet `approved: false` to reject with a note."
          }
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "📊 Credit Scoring",
      "description": "Step 3 of the user flow. Upload financial documents → extract transactions → compute credit score (300–850).\n\n**Supported file formats:** JPEG, PNG, WebP, PDF, CSV, TXT\n**Multiple files:** send multiple `files` fields in one request\n\nThe pipeline:\n1. OCR / text extraction per file\n2. Transaction parsing (Strategy A/B/C/D)\n3. Currency normalization\n4. Categorization (12 categories, EN/AR/TR)\n5. Signal computation (income_level, income_stability, savings_rate, activity, burden)\n6. Score computation (300–850)\n7. Persist + return score",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Upload Financial Documents",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Has score and upload_id', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('upload_id');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('row_count');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('score');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.score).to.have.property('score');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.score).to.have.property('risk_level');",
                  "  console.log('Upload ID:', body.upload_id);",
                  "  console.log('Rows extracted:', body.row_count);",
                  "  console.log('Score:', body.score.score, '|', body.score.risk_level, '|', body.score.score_band);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "files",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Financial document (image/PDF/CSV/TXT, max 25MB). Add multiple 'files' entries for batch upload."
                },
                {
                  "key": "user_country",
                  "value": "YE",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "(Optional) ISO country code for currency conversion (e.g. YE, SA, TR, AE). Defaults to user profile country."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}/credit/upload",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}{{api_prefix}}"],
              "path": ["credit", "upload"]
            },
